<Layout title="About Trade90" description="Trade90 provides source-linked comparisons of central bank rates across 28 forex currency pairs." canonical="/about/">
<main class="wrap"><article class="article"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">About Trade90</span><h1>Clear policy-rate comparisons for traders</h1><p>Trade90 helps readers compare published central-bank interest-rate benchmarks and understand how rate gaps are calculated. Our homepage covers 28 combinations of eight widely traded currencies.</p></header><h2>What we publish</h2><p>Current Rate Gaps use dated, publicly verifiable central-bank rate decisions. Currency Pair Details show the source benchmarks and the signed spread calculation. What Changed separates actual policy decisions from shifts in market expectations.</p><h2>What we do not claim</h2><p>We do not publish unsupported buy/sell signals or claim that a higher policy rate guarantees a stronger currency. Expected-rate values are unavailable until suitable source data can be verified and published transparently.</p><p>Read our <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> or <a href="/contact/">contact us</a> to report an error.</p></article></main>
</Layout>
